    "key_finding": "At N=7 there is NO skyrmion (C_perp=0, generic level spacing Delta~0.23). At N=19 and N=37 the skyrmion sectors show C_perp inside the paper 0.6-0.8 window AND the low-energy structure collapses to a near-degenerate skyrmion/antiskyrmion doublet with tunneling splitting ranging from ~1e-2 down to machine-zero (~1e-14) -- i.e. an EXPONENTIALLY SMALL bandwidth, reproducing the paper headline dynamical claim. The splitting also shows the paper mod-3 selection-rule structure (Nf=2 mod 3 sectors are exactly degenerate = quadratic/vanishing tunneling; Nf=0,1 mod 3 give finite splitting).",
    "paper_claim": "abstract: bandwidth exponentially small from skyrmion<->antiskyrmion tunneling; Nf mod 3 selection rule (paper Fig.7-8)",
